---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy - LifeWebLab',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="px-6 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:py-20 mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <header class="mb-8 md:mb-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold leading-tighter tracking-tighter mb-4 font-heading dark:text-gray-200">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">
        Last updated: October 28, 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
      <p>
        At <strong>LifeWebLab</strong> (accessible from <a href="https://lifeweblab.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">https://lifeweblab.com</a>), the privacy of our visitors is one of our main priorities. This Privacy Policy document outlines the types of information that is collected and recorded by LifeWebLab and how we use it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        LifeWebLab operates as an independent technical publication providing guides on global digital payments, electronic billing, and cross-border payment troubleshooting. We collect non-personally identifiable information automatically via standard web server logs and analytics tools, including browser type, referring/exit pages, operating system, date/time stamps, and clickstream data to diagnose technical issues and optimize reading experiences.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">2. Cookies and Web Beacons</h2>
      <p>
        Like any other modern web platform, LifeWebLab uses 'cookies'. These cookies store information including visitors' preferences, language selection, and accessed pages. This information is utilized to optimize user interactions and customize our technical documentation based on visitors' browser environment and locale settings.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">3. Google AdSense & Advertising Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Google is one of the third-party vendors on our site. It uses advertising cookies (including DART cookies) to serve relevant advertisements to site visitors based upon their visits to LifeWebLab and other web properties. Visitors may choose to decline or opt out of personalized advertising at any time by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Google Ad Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">AboutAds.info</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">4. Third-Party Content & Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We utilize third-party analytics services (such as Google Analytics 4) to monitor website performance and traffic trends. These services may collect technical data sent by your browser during web requests. Third-party ad networks and analytics platforms operate under their respective privacy policies, and LifeWebLab has no direct access to or control over these external tracking mechanisms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">5. Contact Us</h2>
      <!--email_off-->
      <p>
        If you have any questions or require further clarification regarding this Privacy Policy, please reach out directly via our official contact address: <span>contact</span>&#64;<span>lifeweblab.com</span>
      </p>
      <!--/email_off-->
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>